     "span": "It is because the present mind is also unapprehendable.",
     "evidence": "Tibetan ད་ལྟར་བྱུང་བའི་སེམས་ཀྱང་དམིགས་སུ་མེད་པའི་ཕྱིར་རོ། closes the three-part statement (10-1 to 10-3) with the reason particle ཕྱིར་རོ (Skt. tat-kasya hetoḥ ... nopalabhyate); the reason covers past, future and present mind together. The English fragment 'It is because the present mind...' reads as if the reason applies to the present mind alone (cf. Vasubandhu 2-114).",
